DECL	{"args":[{"name":"a","sort":{"sort":"track"}},{"name":"b","sort":{"sort":"track"}}],"body":{"and":[{"and":[{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"},{"lit":"behind"}],"atom":"rel_bearing","params":[]},{"cmp":"lt","lhs":{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"}],"measure":"rel_longitudinal_overlap"},"rhs":{"lit":{"den":1,"num":0},"unit":"metre"}}]},{"and":[{"rises":{"not":{"since":[{"not":{"and":[{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"},{"lit":"behind"}],"atom":"rel_bearing","params":[]},{"cmp":"lt","lhs":{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"}],"measure":"rel_longitudinal_overlap"},"rhs":{"lit":{"den":1,"num":0},"unit":"metre"}}]}},{"and":[{"and":[{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"},{"lit":"ahead"}],"atom":"rel_bearing","params":[]},{"cmp":"lt","lhs":{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"}],"measure":"rel_longitudinal_overlap"},"rhs":{"lit":{"den":1,"num":0},"unit":"metre"}}]},{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"}],"atom":"rel_same_direction","params":[{"param":"same_dir_cos"}]}]}]}}},{"at_last":"time","body":"tt","length":{"param":"window"},"subject":"a","when":{"and":[{"and":[{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"},{"lit":"ahead"}],"atom":"rel_bearing","params":[]},{"cmp":"lt","lhs":{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"}],"measure":"rel_longitudinal_overlap"},"rhs":{"lit":{"den":1,"num":0},"unit":"metre"}}]},{"args":[{"var":"a"},{"var":"b"}],"atom":"rel_same_direction","params":[{"param":"same_dir_cos"}]}]}}]}]},"contract":"Road user a overtakes and passes road user b from the rear: a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it. b is ahead of a where the longitudinal component of b's bearing in a's frame (rel.bearing) is positive and the two bodies' projections on a's heading share no length (rel.longitudinal_overlap negative); b is behind a where that component is negative and the projections share no length. The act begins at the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of a with their headings aligned within same_dir_cos (rel.same_direction). The act is recognized at the observation at which b is behind a and was not behind a at the previous observation, where b was ahead of a with headings aligned at some observation of the window behind. The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until b has again been ahead of a and then comes to be behind it. Conduct before the window behind is not read: a pass that takes longer than the window is not recognized. It denotes the relative motion of the two road users only: it says nothing of the lanes they occupy, of whether b moves, or of why a passes. Not denoted: a drawing alongside b that does not clear b; b ahead of a only while their headings are not aligned (a road user met head-on or crossing); b behind a at every observation of the window.","definition":null,"id":"drv.interaction.overtake_pass","kind":"formula","narrowings":[],"params":[{"name":"window","unit":"second"},{"name":"same_dir_cos","unit":"ratio"}],"residues":[],"supersedes":null}
